robin wrote:
> Please let me know what y'all think of this change.

One thing that makes a the score system tricky here is that it requires 
comparing groups of games against individual games, which is difficult to 
do well.  It is easy to, for example, decide that Fastest Ascension: 
Realtime is worth four times as much as High Score: Caveman, but hard to 
compare Best Behaved Ascension with "ascended two consecutive games" 
(Birdie with Bells On).  Furthermore, the more competitive the tournament 
is [1], the harder is is to win the individual game trophies, but the 
difficulty of multi-game trophies does not change (except best of 13, most 
ascensions, and most unique deaths).  So I'll confine my comments here to 
the point scores for individual games.

Currently:
+ 8 for Fastest Ascension: Gametime 
+ 8 for Fastest Ascension: Realtime 
+ 7 for Best Behaved Ascension 
+ 7 for Lowest Scored Ascension 
+ 6 for First Ascension 
+ 5 for Highest Scored Ascension 
+ 2 for High Score: Role



I suggest:

+ 1 for each ascension, including those counted again later

+ 7 for Fastest Ascension: Gametime
+ 7 for Fastest Ascension: Realtime 
+ 7 for Best Behaved Ascension (even things up)

+ 3 for Lowest Scored Ascension (this is just the Luckiest Pacifist award)
+ 3 for First Ascension (requires both fast play and staying alive, but 
also starting right when the tournament does)
+ 3 for Highest Scored *Game* (if a non-ascension is highest scoring, it 
deserves the award.)

+ 1 for High Score: Role 


If you have time to implement points for runnerups, I suggest:

+5,+3,+2,+1 for 2nd-5th place Fastest Ascension: Gametime
+5,+3,+2,+1 for 2nd-5th place Fastest Ascension: Realtime 
+5,+3,+2,+1 for 2nd-5th place Best Behaved Ascension (

+1 for 2nd Lowest Scored Ascension 
+1 for 2nd First Ascension
+1 for 2nd Highest Scored *Game*







[1] I suspect this year was somewhat less competitive than last year.

